      "content": "Since full squats and deadlifts aren't recommended for the very first week, start this 4-week program with light versions, like goblet squats, push-ups, and dumbbell rows, while you work up to barbell movements. Focus on maintaining perfect form for 3-4 sets of 8-10 reps as you linearly increase your weights by adding 2.5–5 lbs every week once you complete the sets. Track your lifts in a journal or app to ensure you are consistently challenging yourself, but remember your primary goals are learning movement patterns, not heavy strength gains yet.",
