      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a simplified 4-week linear progression plan focusing on a full-body split worked out Monday, Wednesday, and Friday:\n\n*   **Weeks 1-2:** Start with empty bar or very light weights. Do Goblet Squats (3x8), Push-Ups (3x10, assume knees or incline if needed), Romanian Deadlifts (3x8), Bench Press (3x8), and Dumbbell Rows (3x10). Add 2.5 lbs to all lifts once you hit the 3rd set easily.\n*   **Weeks 3-4:** Progress to standard Barbell Back Squats, Barbell Bench Press, and Barbell Deadlifts. Maintain the 3x8-10 rep scheme and continue adding 2.5–5 lbs whenever your 3 sets feel achievable before your last set.\n*   **Rest Days:** Take Tuesday, Thursday, Saturday, and Sunday off to allow your muscles to recover fully. Prioritize sleep and hydration to aid recovery. Stick to this exact schedule for four weeks, and adjust weights only when your current weight feels too easy for three full sets.",
